(* A–Z mixing for HEFT.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   This module is the dedicated place to compute

     - AZnorm  : 2×2 mixing matrix between (W^3, B) and (Z, A), (W^3, B)^T = AZnorm . (Z, A)^T

   as a function of the active operators P1 and P12, at FIRST ORDER in WCOrder: the model keeps a
   single EFT insertion per vertex (fixed since 2026-09-17), so AZnorm is linear in CP1n0 and
   CP12n0 and written out explicitly below - no Series, no square roots of EFT coefficients.
   AZnorm is *used* in `fields.fr` via the `Definitions` of the unphysical gauge fields `B` and
   `Wi`.

   Which operators enter.  There are no Wnorm / Bnorm / Gnorm any more (removed 2026-09-16): PG,
   PB and PW use Fbar(h) = F(h) - 1 (nmin = 1, 1604.06801 eqs. C.14-C.16), so they vanish at h = 0
   and never touch the gauge kinetic terms, and gw :> GW, g1 :> G1, gs :> GS carry no
   normalisation.  Only P1 (W3-B kinetic mixing, S) and P12 (W3 kinetic rescaling, U) modify the
   kinetic matrix; their h^0 parts are physical, so F-bar is not available for them.

   Derivation.  With TT = PauliSigma[3] and FSWi = sigma^a W^a/2 (definitions.fr),
   Tr[TT.FSWi] = W3_{mu nu}, so in L = -1/4 V^T K V, V = (W3, B),

       K = {{1 - 4 x c12, -2 x c1}, {-2 x c1, 1}},    x = WCOrder, c1 = CP1n0, c12 = CP12n0.

   AZnorm = diag(P12normINV, 1) . M . R(theta) makes X^T K X = 1 and the photon massless:
     - W3 rescaling   P12normINV = 1/Sqrt[1 - 4 x c12]            = 1 + 2 x c12
     - mixing         eps = -2 x c1 P12normINV                    = -2 x c1       (c12 drops out)
     - de-mixing      M = {{a, 0}, {c, 1}}, a = 1/Sqrt[1-eps^2]   = 1,  c = -eps = 2 x c1
     - rotation       cos(theta) = (GW + eps G1 P12norm)/Sqrt[GW^2 + 2 eps GW G1 P12norm + P12norm^2 G1^2]
                                 = cW + 2 x sW^2 (c12 cW - c1 sW)
                      sin(theta) = sW - 2 x sW cW (c12 cW - c1 sW)
   with cW = GW/Sqrt[GW^2+G1^2], sW = G1/Sqrt[GW^2+G1^2] (every "=" on the right is at first
   order in x).  Multiplying out and dropping x^2 gives the four entries below.  At x = 0, or with
   neither P1 nor P12 selected, they are exactly the SM rotation {{cW, sW}, {-sW, cW}} - so there
   is no separate SM branch.  P1 and P12 contribute independently: no c1 c12 term survives at one
   insertion.  Checked against the previous Series-based construction for all four P1/P12
   selections, and X^T K X = 1 + O(x^2), massless photon to O(x) (TESTS.md T31).

   History (the signs and factors above are the result of two fixes in the former exact /
   Series-based construction, kept here because the explicit form inherits them):
     - FIXED 2026-08-12: eps read -4 x c1 instead of -2 x c1.  The kinetic terms were then not
       canonically normalised - X^T K X - I left a residual A-Z kinetic mixing
       2 x c1 (GW^2-G1^2)/(G1^2+GW^2) - and the mass sector could not catch it, because the photon
       mass and the A-Z mass mixing vanish identically for any eps.
     - FIXED 2026-08-13: M had an overall minus sign (M = -I at eps = 0), which flipped (Z, A)
       relative to a run without P1/P12 and made the extracted photon coupling come out as -e.
     - 2026-09-17: the exact square-root construction, expanded with Series, was replaced by
       these explicit first-order entries (identical at first order). *)

(* Main hook: called from HEFT_Model.fr before assembling the full Lagrangian. *)

HEFTUpdateGaugeNormalizations[] :=
    Module[{c1, c12, cW, sW},
      If[True,
        c1  = If[ValueQ[HEFTActiveEFTPieces] && HEFTPieceActiveQ["P1"],  CP1n0,  0];
        c12 = If[ValueQ[HEFTActiveEFTPieces] && HEFTPieceActiveQ["P12"], CP12n0, 0];
        cW = GW/Sqrt[GW^2 + G1^2];
        sW = G1/Sqrt[GW^2 + G1^2];
        AZnorm1x1aux =  cW + 2*WCOrder*(c12*cW*(1 + sW^2) - c1*sW^3);
        AZnorm1x2aux =  sW + 2*WCOrder*sW^2*(c12*sW + c1*cW);
        AZnorm2x1aux = -sW + 2*WCOrder*cW^2*(c12*sW + c1*cW);
        AZnorm2x2aux =  cW + 2*WCOrder*sW*cW*(c12*sW + c1*cW);
      ];
    ];
